agentic-code-reviewers v0.4.0 (cursor-sdk)

⚠️ **WARNING:** MemoryAdapter returns caller-facing payloads without the same sanitizeToolOutput pass used by MCP tools. readMemoryBootstrap forwards compileBootstrapBrief directly, so traps/decisions/activeSlice MemoRecord objects still carry absolute vault paths in their path fields and any credential-like strings in bodies/frontmatter are not redacted. updateMemoryTrap and updateMemoryLog also return raw UpsertResult/AppendResult objects with absolute path values. This recreates the vault-path and read-path secret leakage that was fixed on the MCP seam, but through the Phase 2 harness entrypoint exported from index.ts.

**Correção sugerida:**

```ts
import { sanitizeToolOutput } from './safety.js';
import { BootstrapBrief, AppendResult } from './types.js';

async readMemoryBootstrap(cwd: string, query?: string): Promise<BootstrapBrief> {
  const brief = await compileBootstrapBrief({ cwd, query, vaultRoot: this.vaultRoot });
  return sanitizeToolOutput(brief) as BootstrapBrief;
}

async updateMemoryTrap(...): Promise<UpsertResult> {
  const result = await upsertRecord({ /* unchanged args */ });
  return sanitizeToolOutput(result) as UpsertResult;
}

async updateMemoryLog(...): Promise<AppendResult> {
  const result = await appendEvent({ /* unchanged args */ });
  return sanitizeToolOutput(result) as AppendResult;
}
```

<details>
<summary>🔍 Detalhes da Análise IA</summary>

**Score:** 8/10 | **Ação dev:** fix-code

**Análise:**
1. Evidence: src/adapter.ts readMemoryBootstrap (lines 23-28) returns compileBootstrapBrief unchanged; updateMemoryTrap/updateMemoryLog return upsertRecord/appendEvent results with path (lines 38-53, 58-64). src/tools.ts ok() wraps all MCP responses with sanitizeToolOutput (lines 237-238, 262-266). src/compiler.ts scanProjectRecords attaches absolute filePath to each MemoRecord.path (lines 32-36). 2. Scenario: A workflow-skills consumer calls MemoryAdapter.readMemoryBootstrap and receives traps[].path like $SPEC_MEMO_ROOT/projects/<id>/traps/foo.md; a trap body containing a stored GitHub token is echoed verbatim to the host agent context. 3. Protection: src/tools.test.ts and src/mcp.test.ts verify MCP sanitization, but src/adapter.test.ts never asserts path omission or secret redaction and even asserts res.path.includes(tempVaultRoot) for updateMemoryTrap. 4. Discards: Not the same as the resolved MCP search/upsert path leak (those go through executeTool); this is a separate adapter code path that bypasses the fix.

**Caminhos analisados:** /src/adapter.ts, /src/adapter.test.ts, /src/tools.ts, /src/safety.ts, /src/bootstrap.ts, /src/compiler.ts, /src/index.ts
</details>

