agentic-code-reviewers v0.4.0 (cursor-sdk)

⚠️ **WARNING:** Vault mutation serialization is only enforced for upsertRecord via withVaultLock. appendEvent, forgetRecord, and runGc perform read-modify-write and index rebuild operations without acquiring the same .memo.lock, so they can interleave with an in-flight upsert (including trap deduplication and supersede updates). Two concurrent CLI/MCP processes can therefore archive or purge a trap while upsert is scanning traps, or rebuild the FTS index while upsert is indexing, producing duplicate active traps, stale supersede links, or transient search gaps.

**Correção sugerida:**

```ts
export async function forgetRecord(options: ForgetOptions): Promise<ForgetResult> {
  const vaultRoot = options.vaultRoot || getVaultRoot();
  return withVaultLock(vaultRoot, async () => {
    // existing forgetRecord body
  });
}

export async function appendEvent(options: AppendOptions): Promise<AppendResult> {
  const vaultRoot = options.vaultRoot || getVaultRoot();
  return withVaultLock(vaultRoot, async () => {
    // existing appendEvent body
  });
}

export async function runGc(options: GcOptions = {}): Promise<GcResult> {
  const vaultRoot = options.vaultRoot || getVaultRoot();
  return withVaultLock(vaultRoot, async () => {
    // existing runGc body
  });
}
```

<details>
<summary>🔍 Detalhes da Análise IA</summary>

**Score:** 7/10 | **Ação dev:** fix-code

**Análise:**
1. Evidence: grep shows withVaultLock is used only in src/store.ts upsertRecord (line 100) and internally in commitVaultChange (vault.ts:315). appendEvent (store.ts:331), forgetRecord (store.ts:405), and runGc (curator.ts:91) mutate markdown/SQLite/compiled views without the lock. vault.ts documents file lock across processes (lines 49-66, 93-94). 2. Scenario: Process A starts upsertRecord(kind:'trap'), acquires .memo.lock, reads active traps for dedup; Process B calls forgetRecord(purge:true) on one of those traps without locking and deletes the file; Process A completes and writes a new active trap referencing supersedes:<deleted-id>, leaving duplicate or inconsistent trap state. Alternatively, runGc rebuildIndex deletes/rebuilds FTS while upsert indexRecord runs. 3. Protection: No concurrent/integration tests in store.test.ts, curator.test.ts, or adapter.test.ts; prior trap-dedup lock fix covered upsert only. 4. Discards: Single-process reentrancy is handled by lock depth; this finding requires parallel processes or mixed gc/forget/upsert calls.

**Caminhos analisados:** /src/store.ts, /src/curator.ts, /src/vault.ts, /src/indexer.ts
</details>

