agentic-code-reviewers v0.4.0 (cursor-sdk)

💡 **SUGGESTION:** There is no automated coverage that MemoryAdapter applies the same read-path sanitization contract as MCP tools. adapter.test.ts only checks functional behavior and even asserts that updateMemoryTrap returns a path inside the temp vault, which codifies vault-path leakage rather than guarding against regressions of the host-neutral output policy.

**Correção sugerida:**

```ts
it('should omit vault paths and redact secrets in adapter bootstrap output', async () => {
  await adapter.updateMemoryTrap(process.cwd(), {
    scenario: 'Secret trap',
    doNot: 'leak',
    insteadDo: 'redact',
    severity: 'high'
  });
  const brief = await adapter.readMemoryBootstrap(process.cwd());
  assert.equal(JSON.stringify(brief).includes(tempVaultRoot), false);
  for (const trap of brief.traps) {
    assert.equal((trap as { path?: string }).path, undefined);
  }
});
```

<details>
<summary>🔍 Detalhes da Análise IA</summary>

**Score:** 6/10 | **Ação dev:** fix-code

**Análise:**
1. Evidence: adapter.test.ts lines 24-44 lack assertions that brief.traps[].path is undefined or that secrets are redacted; line 43 explicitly expects res.path to include tempVaultRoot. MCP coverage exists in tools.test.ts (lines 125-151) but adapter is a separate exported surface (index.ts:14). 2. Scenario: A refactor removes sanitizeToolOutput from adapter methods; CI stays green because adapter tests never check omission/redaction. 3. Protection: tools.test.ts covers MCP only; safety.test.ts covers write-path assertNoSecrets only. 4. Discards: This is not claiming sanitization is absent (that is filed separately on adapter.ts); this finding is the missing regression net.

**Caminhos analisados:** /src/adapter.test.ts, /src/tools.test.ts, /src/safety.test.ts, /src/adapter.ts
</details>

